{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3305","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3305","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3305\",\"parent_revision\":\"376efb9e2e3f4fef156eb65429467d54b83d149aa9a715bebcdedd6c9aa2cdab\",\"root_revision\":\"376efb9e2e3f4fef156eb65429467d54b83d149aa9a715bebcdedd6c9aa2cdab\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-29\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nDuring /dh:implement-feature's step 4a, three bare Agent(subagent_type=\\\"dh:contract-verification\\\") dispatches were made in the same worktree-isolated session that had already edited plugins/development-harness/agents/contract-verification.md (task T1 of plan P7ac7ec69). One of them (verify-T1) reported three CONTRACT VIOLATION and two CONTRACT GAP findings claiming the file still had the pre-fix content: still declaring only 3 inputs (architect_spec_path, task_id, modified_files \u2014 the exact old field list, not a paraphrase), still containing the dead line 'Your finding is your response...', and still granting SendMessage in the tools: frontmatter line.\\n\\nDirectly verified against the worktree file at the time verify-T1 ran (via grep from the orchestrator's own Bash tool, same working directory): none of these were true. The file already had all of T1's fixes \u2014 a 4th input field (issue_number), the dead line replaced with a backlog_groom Delivery section, and SendMessage removed from tools:. The orchestrator's Bash/Grep tool calls and the dispatched subagent's task-worker siblings (T1/T2/T3, dispatched the same way via bare Agent()) all correctly read/wrote the worktree copy \u2014 git status and git diff after their completion matched exactly what they reported.\\n\\nImpact: contract-verification's findings (step 4a of implement-feature) cannot be trusted at face value when dispatched via bare Agent() in a worktree-isolated session \u2014 a false CONTRACT VIOLATION was written to the backlog item's Concerns section (since struck, with a note, after manual verification) and would otherwise have been picked up as a genuine defect by /complete-implementation's validation stage, potentially spawning a spurious follow-up backlog item against already-correct work.\\n\\n**Hypothesis**: the specific mechanism (session-cwd resolution, a stale read-cache, or the subagent conflating the architect spec's quoted 'before' text with a fresh read of the current file \u2014 the architect spec for #3276 literally quotes the old line 151 text verbatim as part of explaining what needed to change) is not confirmed. Root-causing which of these applies (or whether it is specific to dh:contract-verification's own instructions vs. a broader bare-Agent()-in-worktree issue) is left to grooming/RT-ICA.\\n\\nNot yet verified: whether this reproduces for non-self-referential targets (i.e., contract-verification checking some OTHER file it didn't just edit itself), or whether dh:task-worker-family dispatches are immune only by coincidence of this specific test, or by some real difference in how they establish working context.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 2026-08-29, while running /dh:implement-feature step 4a for plan P7ac7ec69 (#3276), dispatching dh:contract-verification against the just-fixed contract-verification.md itself as a self-test\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-29\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-29T08:45:53.725457Z</sub>\\n\\n## Second occurrence \u2014 dh:doc-drift-auditor (2026-08-29, QG plan P6494befe/T4)\\n\\nSame symptom, different agent type: `dh:doc-drift-auditor`, dispatched via bare `Agent()` as `/complete-implementation`'s QG T4 (Documentation Drift Audit), registered an `audit-report` artifact for #3276 claiming 7 drift items (2 critical) \u2014 all citing pre-fix text verbatim as if still current: `contract-verification.md` line 151 (\\\"Your finding is your response...\\\"), the `SendMessage` tools grant, and `implement-feature/SKILL.md`'s old `<concerns>`-block dispatch branch. All three were removed by commits `757101daa`/`d6977e693`/`51b4cd1f3` on the same branch before T4 ran.\\n\\nDirectly verified against the live worktree with absolute-path grep at the time T4's report was reviewed: zero occurrences of any of the quoted \\\"current\\\" text in any of the 4 audited files. The audit's recommended fix (re-add SendMessage) would have reverted the actual implemented fix.\\n\\nOrchestrator overrode the mechanical \\\"findings > 0 \u2192 dispatch T5 Documentation Update\\\" QG gate rather than let a documentation-update agent \\\"fix\\\" already-correct docs based on this false audit \u2014 details recorded in QG plan P6494befe's context field. T5 marked `skipped` with justification, not dispatched.\\n\\nThis strengthens the original hypothesis toward \\\"broader bare-Agent()-in-worktree issue\\\" over \\\"specific to dh:contract-verification's own instructions\\\" (the two candidate causes named in the original report) \u2014 the symptom now spans two structurally different agent types (a verification agent and an audit agent) dispatched the same way in the same worktree session.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"88df32009a08b533d8fec3d05866066dd8a5a0f301882f44a0c913c5f4cd11de\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABRYX-ZQ\"}"}